summary_en="Starting from the question of why the “fastest route” suggested by a navigation system felt so uncomfortable, this essay considers the questions humans must ask in the face of machines that know the answers. It proposes “integrative intelligence,” built on the three pillars of scientific literacy, humanistic reflection, and social participation, as the core of the kind of person education should aim to develop in the age of AI, and outlines the changes needed in schools and in policy.",
